From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom-smbchg: report the actual AICL error

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/msm8953-mainline/linux
License: GPL-2.0-only (modified upstream sources)
Base-commit: 755ffc44d5d8442adeec8bbaa02108478089c4d7

smbchg_handle_aicl_done() stores the result of smbchg_usb_get_ilim() in
ilim, but its failure message uses an uninitialized ret instead. Report
the actual negative result and remove the unused local variable.

This fixes the compiler warning and preserves the interrupt handler's
control flow and charger behavior.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
@@ -1116,13 +1116,12 @@ static irqreturn_t smbchg_handle_aicl_done(int irq, void *data)
 {
 	struct smbchg_chip *chip = data;
 	int ilim;
-	int ret;
 
 	dev_dbg(chip->dev, "AICL done");
 
 	ilim = smbchg_usb_get_ilim(chip);
 	if (ilim < 0)
 		dev_warn(chip->dev, "Failed to read AICL result: %pe\n",
-			 ERR_PTR(ret));
+			 ERR_PTR(ilim));
 	else
 		dev_dbg(chip->dev, "AICL result: %uuA", ilim);
